  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening advocacy for resilience through environmental conservation &amp; sustainable agricultural</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the spirit of &quot;our common home&quot; strategy and envisioning Kenya and Uganda Resilience Programme, Kenya Conference of Catholic Bishops (KCCB) has proposed  &#x201c;Strengthening advocacy for resilience and poverty eradication through environmental conservation and sustainable agricultural productivity&#x201d; to be implemented by the Catholic Justice and Peace  Department (KCCB-CJPD) both at the national level and in select  Counties. The project seeks to understand policy provisions and targets to engage state and non-state actors on environment, natural resources management, climate change and empower local communities to engage both national and county governments through advocacy - Citizen Voices and Actions. 
This project commenced in 2022, KCCB CJPD designed this project informed by CAFOD strategic direction &quot;Our Common Home&quot;. The plan was to transition successful advocacy work, structures/groups and engagement, information  focus to include environmental management and climate change. In year 2 KCCB CJPD  carried out a research to assess and understand legal and policy contest on climate change and environment. Research findings  and context analysis has informed project design for year two and three whose result areas include; 
Programme Goal: To contribute towards building resilient communities to adapt to the impacts of climate change in the ASAL counties of Isiolo, Marsabit, Samburu and Kericho Counties 
Specific Objectives: 
1.	To Foster collaboration and partnerships among local communities and other stakeholders to support climate change resilience and sustainability 
2.	To strengthen the capacity of the communities to implement climate change adaptation and mitigation initiatives and to enhance ecological spirituality through evangelization</narrative>
  </description>
